{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Hex Map",
  "theme": "hexdash",
  "mapLive": true,
  "_about": "After BMW's Live Cockpit Sport view with the map in the middle, generated by tools/gen_hexmap.py (edit that and regenerate). One hexdash effect layer draws the black backdrop and a hexagon frame of two brackets (speed left 0..200 mph, revs right 0..7000), each a white outer line, a band lit red to orange up to the value and an orange inner line, closed by their top and bottom runs. While the Waze map shows inside the theme ('Show Waze map inside the theme', 'mapUp'), the hexagon's inside is cut see-through over the map, only within BMW's map window (416,120 1088x480), without a rebuild (mapLive); otherwise a road runs in it. Speed, fuel and range outside on the left, gear, drive mode and oil temperature on the right, boost and coolant under the hexagon, the clock and outside temperature in the bottom strip, BMW's gear letter left uncovered. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
